  "findings": [
    "Actual builtin changed-path set is copied before the forwarded operation. Only fixed path categories and SHA256 digests escape; raw home/path content does not. None and empty sets retain the actual marker branch, database plus control marker retains the source-declared marker branch, control-only retains compilation, and other metadata retains force classification.",
    "The new database marker wrapper calls the original once. It exports only null, the exact fixed unavailable label, or a validated 64-lowerhex digest; arbitrary return values fault the recorder while preserving original return/exception.",
    "Private marker sampling uses the existing nonblocking publisher condition read and no getter or new file/database operation. Marker writes in product are not all guarded by this condition, so the record remains a read interval, not an atomic commit or complete state transition.",
    "The two caller-provider additions bind real original code objects. Negative old-registry and positive expanded-registry controls exercise actual publication_context, prepare_native_hook_policy and failure-reason caller functions.",
    "The original lifecycle closes and checks its publisher before dispatch returns; the reader requires publisher_contained and rejects active/lost/unknown/incomplete records. No new thread wait is added by this delta.",
    "The original 400ms acceptance and existing original calls remain unchanged; observation overhead lies inside affected intervals and is not clean performance evidence. Argument branches are source classifications, not historical cause proof."
  ],
